iness are  undergoing such a dramatic change how  they are going to present content and  the basis the flexibility is beyond  anything that any of us could ever have  imagined but I know AT&amp;T personally I  know their leadership they'll get it  done they're one of the most admired by  me people on this and in the country and  the NFL wants to be a big part of a team  team's future and I think about the  valuation of your own team Gerry do you  think it's it's correctly value  particularly after today's contract  extension well I think this no one knows  what something is worth until the  marketplace until it's sold if you will  or bought that won't be the case for the  Dallas Cowboys I know that I would trade  a lot of those evaluations for more  first downs or more game wins at the end  of the day I didn't get into football to  make money I got into football to  compete and compete for Super Bowls on  the other hand it's with great pride  that we run the team and that we run it  in a way that has that kind of  recognition well did you get into  natural gas to make money because there  is 75% owner obviously of Comstock  resources and natural gas has been stuck  at around 3 $3 50 but that's well below  the $6 you need to actually be  profitable where do you see natural gas  prices well I think that of course  natural gas to be tried is a commodity  on the other hand it has all of the  things that you look for in commodities  it has to be in the right location the  cost of it either grow it or produce it  has to be really efficient to long term  make money comstock are joining with  Covey Park the place that we drilled the  leases that we have is the most  efficient place in the world to have  natural gas and our market is right  there and so we don't have very far to  go to get it and nowadays you get to  have ngl which is exported starting in  about 16 our country started exporting  the products of natural gas which is ng  this is what sparked my interest I got 